========================================================================================================================
HPE VM ESSENTIALS (VME) & VME MANAGER - NETWORK TROUBLESHOOTING CHEATSHEET
========================================================================================================================

1. CENTRAL VME MANAGER (APPLIANCE-LEVEL DIAGNOSTICS)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CATEGORY               COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IP & Gateway Valid.    ip a                                            Confirm local appliance interface IP assignments
IP & Gateway Valid.    ip route                                        Inspect active default gateways and interface tables
DNS & URL Mapping      hostname -f                                     Verify current Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN)
DNS & URL Mapping      nslookup $(hostname -f)                         Ensure DNS maps matching record targets (CRITICAL)
DNS & URL Mapping      nslookup <Appliance_IP_Address>                 Test reverse DNS lookup pointers for the system

Morpheus Service Stack sudo morpheus-ctl status                        Verify if central rabbitmq, ui, and DB rings are UP
Morpheus Service Stack sudo morpheus-ctl restart morpheus-ui           Restart only the web console rendering pipeline
Morpheus Service Stack sudo morpheus-ctl reconfigure                   Force rebuild application network templates

Live Payload Streams   tail -f /var/log/morpheus/morpheus-ui/current   Monitor active incoming agent API connections
Live Payload Streams   tail -f /var/log/morpheus/nginx/error.log       Check reverse proxy dropouts or failed UI bindings

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. VME NODES / HVM HOST NETWORK VERIFICATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CATEGORY               COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Link Verification      sudo ip link set <interface_name> up            Wake dropped physical NICs (e.g., post-host-reboot)
Link Verification      sudo netplan get                                Fetch live active netplan profile block parameters
Link Verification      sudo netplan try                                Test adjustments with an automated 120s safety rollback

Inter-Node Routing     nc -zv <Manager_IP> 443                         Test if node can reach central VME Manager API port
Inter-Node Routing     nc -zv <Target_Node_IP> 22                      Verify node-to-node private SSH key sync loops
Inter-Node Routing     ping -M do -s 8972 <Storage_IP>                 Test Jumbo Frames path capability (MTU 9000 check)

Plugin & Fabric Logs   tail -f /var/log/hvm/network-plugin.log         Stream v9+ decoupled Open vSwitch plug-in bindings
Plugin & Fabric Logs   tail -f /var/log/libvirt/libvirtd.log          Track libvirt virtual function (VF) and tap leaks
Wipe & Start Over      sudo /opt/hpe-vm/scripts/reset_host.sh          Purge a broken, misconfigured node net-layer
